Independent review of `spec:pose-review-run-reaps-lingering-reviewer-processes`

decision: changes-requested

Findings:

- **N1 — medium, blocker** — [pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_reap_other.go:8). The non-Linux fallback says process-group termination is available, but Windows implements both process-group functions as no-ops ([review_dispatch_windows.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch_windows.go:14)). A Windows review can leave a child alive while dispatch continues into worktree checks and cleanup. The manuals repeat this inaccurate platform claim.
- **N2 — low, follow-up** — [pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_shim_linux.go:167). A PID is recorded as ended when SIGKILL delivery succeeds, before the reaper confirms it exited. If it remains alive past the bound, the run record still lists it as ended alongside a generic incomplete-reap error.
- **N3 — low, follow-up** — [pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4083797052/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_dispatch.go:1130). When more than 1,001 PIDs are reported, the dispatch uses the capped PID list plus a single “and N more” entry to calculate the headline count, so it reports 1,001 regardless of the larger total.

Validation: the focused tests, focused race tests, the adapter exit-status test, and focused `go vet` passed. Both strict validate commands were attempted but failed before Go checks because the read-only sandbox denied Go temporary build/cache writes; sealed build, e2e, integration and unit evidence is used for those tools. `surface-check` passed with 0 findings. `artifact-check` exited 0 but resolved change set `cs-06c6af066283` (head `3994f49`), rather than the brief’s `cs-cd7b2a0ff10a`, and emitted 988 orphan warnings, so I did not treat it as scoped attribution evidence. Tech-debt assessment was incomplete due to two unrelated invalid specs and an uncovered panic in `bounded_cache.go`. Closeout and review checks are deferred because they require an attestation, which this task forbids.

The sweep covered the Linux shim/reaper and fallback paths, dispatch/report lifecycle, attempt release and ledger flow, CLI/help contract, review-brief template, English and PT-BR manuals and scaffold copies, and the associated regression tests. Rules applied: `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/backend-go.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`. No repository changes or attestations were made.

